{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require police to conduct Animal Welfare Checks on pets when Owner is in Custody",
        "additional_details": "Where an individual is taken into custody and their animal is left at home without any available friend, family member to provide care, a welfare check must be arranged if the period of the owner\u2019s absence exceeds four hours. The check must establish that the animal is safe, has access to fresh drinking water and suitable conditions, has been fed, and is not showing signs of distress or neglect. Any concerns must be recorded and appropriate action taken to safeguard the animal\u2019s welfare.",
        "background": "When an owner is in custody and their animal home alone, steps must be taken to ensure the animal\u2019s welfare is not compromised. A compulsory welfare check must be initiated after 4-hours, with further action taken according to the animal\u2019s needs and the anticipated duration of the owner\u2019s detention.",
